.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt MAN 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm man
.Nd display manual pages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl acfhklw
.Op Fl C Ar file
.Op Fl M Ar path
.Op Fl m Ar path
.Op Fl S Ar subsection
.Op Oo Fl s Oc Ar section
.Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility finds the manual page for each
.Ar name ,
formats it with
.Xr oxdoc 1
and shows it through a pager.
.Pp
Without a
.Ar section ,
the sections are searched in the order 1, 8, 6, 2, 3, 5, 7, 4, 9, and the
first page found is shown.
A
.Ar section
may also be given as the first argument when a name follows it, as in
.Ql man 8 init .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Show every matching page, not only the first.
.It Fl C Ar file
Read
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /etc/man.conf .
.It Fl c
Do not use a pager.
.It Fl f
The same as
.Xr whatis 1 .
.It Fl h
Show only the SYNOPSIS section.
.It Fl k
The same as
.Xr apropos 1 .
.It Fl l
The arguments are file names, not page names.
.It Fl M Ar path
Search the colon-separated manual directories in
.Ar path
instead of the default.
.It Fl m Ar path
Search the directories in
.Ar path
before the others.
.It Fl S Ar subsection
Look in the architecture subdirectory
.Ar subsection ,
by default the machine's.
.It Fl s Ar section
Only search
.Ar section .
.It Fl w
Print the file names of the pages instead of showing them.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl T ,
.Fl O
and
.Fl W
options of
.Xr oxdoc 1
are also accepted and passed on.
.Pp
A page is found in a manual directory by any of the names its NAME section
gives, through the directory's index,
.Pa oxdoc.db ,
which
.Xr makewhatis 8
builds; so
.Ql man less
finds
.Pa more.1 .
Otherwise, or without an index, a page is found as
.Pa man Ns Ar N Ns / Ns Ar name . Ns Ar section ,
where
.Ar N
is the first character of the section, or in the architecture
subdirectory of that directory.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MANPAGER
.It Ev MANPAGER
The pager, run with
.Pa /bin/sh
.Fl c .
.It Ev MANPATH
The manual directories, separated by colons.
A colon at the start or end, or two together, stand for the directories
.Pa /etc/man.conf
names.
.It Ev PAGER
The pager if
.Ev MANPAGER
is not set; the default is
.Ql /usr/bin/more -s .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/man.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/man.conf
the manual directories
.It Pa /usr/share/man
the system's manual pages
.It Pa oxdoc.db
the index in each manual directory
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success, and 5 if a page was not found or the
arguments were wrong.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr apropos 1 ,
.Xr more 1 ,
.Xr oxdoc 1 ,
.Xr man.conf 5 ,
.Xr man 7 ,
.Xr mdoc 7 ,
.Xr makewhatis 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v2 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
